<title>ARGENTINA: LatAm stocks seen firm in week, focused on profits.</title>
<headline>LatAm stocks seen firm in week, focused on profits.</headline>
<byline>Carmen Pignotti</byline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latin American bolsas were seen cheerful on carnival week, with most stocks driven higher by a good reporting season, dealers said.</p>
<p>The markets of Brazil and Venezuela will remain closed Monday and Tuesday for carnival celebrations, while Chile's bolsa was expected to grab the spotlight at the start of the week.</p>
<p>Chilean stocks surged 3.8 percent Friday on news of the Central Bank's surprise decision Thursday to trim interest rates, halting its year-long policy of tight credit.</p>
</text>
